<table class="fileinfotpl-type-information vevent" dir="ltr">

<tbody><tr>
<td id="fileinfotpl&#95;desc" class="fileinfo-paramfield" lang="en">Description<span class="summary fn" style="display:none">Castello di Miramare - Trieste.jpg</span></td>
<td class="description">
<div class="description it" dir="ltr" lang="it"><span class="language it" title="Italian"><b>Italiano&#58; </b></span> Castello di Miramare circondato dalla riserva naturale visto dalla passeggiata Napoleoniva, che dall'obelisco giunge sino a Prosecco e che domina la riviera di Barcola.</div>
<div class="description en" dir="ltr" lang="en"><span class="language en" title="English"><b>English&#58; </b></span> Miramare Castle surrounded by the nature reserve seen from the Napoleoniva promenade, which from the obelisk reaches Prosecco and dominates the Barcola Riviera.</div><table cellspacing="0" style="width:50%; text-align:left; color:inherit; background:var(--background-color-content-added,#A4DCFF); border:1px solid var(--border-color-progressive--active,#191970); margin:1px;" dir="ltr" class="layouttemplate">
<tbody><tr><td style="width:22px; height:22px;"><span class="noviewer" typeof="mw:File"><a href="/wiki/File:Italy_looking_like_the_flag.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img src="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Italy_looking_like_the_flag.svg/20px-Italy_looking_like_the_flag.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="20" height="24" class="mw-file-element" srcset="https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Italy_looking_like_the_flag.svg/40px-Italy_looking_like_the_flag.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="738" data-file-height="870" /></a></span></td>
<td style="font-size:8pt; padding:1pt; line-height:1.1em;" lang="en">
<p>This is a photo of a monument which is part of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_heritage" class="extiw" title="en:Cultural heritage">cultural heritage</a> of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italy" class="extiw" title="en:Italy">Italy</a>. This monument participates in the contest <a href="https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progetto:Wiki_Loves_Monuments_2018" class="extiw" title="it:Progetto:Wiki Loves Monuments 2018">Wiki Loves Monuments Italia 2018</a>. See <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://workspace.wikimedia.it/s/7wQqJ87Cy2b55oR">authorisations</a>. <small>(wiki-ID: <span class="plainlinks"><a class="external text" href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=haswbstatement%3AP2186%3D03200633&amp;fulltext=Search&amp;ns102=1">03200633</a></span>)</small>
</p>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<table cellspacing="8" cellpadding="0" style="width:100%; clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; background-color:#f7f8ff; border:2px solid #66A7CC;" class="plainlinks" dir="ltr">
<tbody><tr>
<td style="width:60px">
</td>
<td style="text-align:center;"><div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="description en" style="display:inline;">The authorisation for taking photos of this object was provided by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:World_Wide_Fund_for_Nature" class="extiw" title="w:en:World Wide Fund for Nature">World Wide Fund for Nature Italy</a>.</div>
</td></tr></tbody></table></td>
